<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<title>wrong api path page</title>
</head>
<body>
<script>
// The right host and token, but the token is followed by a trailing segment:
// under the token-anchored match, '/vouchers/groups/{token}/extra' is NOT the
// voucher endpoint and must never be captured. (The live API sits under a
// version prefix such as '/v1/public/', so a pure prefix check is no longer
// the correct rejection test - the token-anchored shape is.)
fetch('/vouchers/groups/WrongPathFetch/extra');
</script>
</body>
</html>
